# MBREMS (Multi-Branch Restaurant Management System)

Team project with 4 members. I am MEMBER 4: Customer Experience & Business Intelligence.
Only work inside my areas unless I say otherwise.

## Stack (JavaScript only, no TypeScript, no SQL)
- Frontend: React (Vite), React Router, Axios, Leaflet (map), Recharts (analytics)
- Backend: Node.js, Express, Mongoose (CommonJS: require/module.exports)
- Database: MongoDB Atlas
- Auth: JWT. Token payload is { id, role }. Roles: owner, admin, manager, employee, supplier, delivery, customer
- Root uses `concurrently` to run client and server with `npm run dev`

## Folder structure
mbrems/
  package.json (root, concurrently)
  client/src/api/axios.js (axios instance, adds JWT from localStorage 'token')
  client/src/modules/customer/ (MY frontend code: pages, components)
  server/server.js, config/db.js, middleware/auth.js, models/, controllers/, routes/, scripts/
Other members own: client/src/modules/core (M1), inventory (M2), operations (M3).

## My modules (Member 4)
1. Customer management (profiles, addresses, preferences, order history)
2. Online ordering interface (browse, cart, checkout, order tracking)
3. Delivery management (staff assignment, status, history)
4. Simulated GPS tracking (predefined coordinates, marker moves on Leaflet map, polling every 3s, no WebSockets)
5. Marketing and promotions (coupons, campaigns)
6. Customer service and feedback (ratings, reviews, complaints)
7. Reports and analytics (branch sales, revenue, orders, delivery performance, charts)

## My Mongoose models
Customer (user ref, phone, addresses[], preferences{dietary[], favouriteBranch}, loyaltyPoints)
Coupon (code, discountType percent|fixed, discountValue, minOrderAmount, maxDiscount, validFrom, validTo, usageLimit, usedCount, branches[], isActive)
Delivery (order ref unique, deliveryStaff ref Employee, status pending|assigned|picked_up|on_the_way|delivered|cancelled, pickup{lat,lng}, dropoff{lat,lng}, route[], currentIndex, assignedAt, deliveredAt)
Review (customer, order, branch, foodRating 1-5, deliveryRating 1-5, comment; unique index customer+order)
Complaint (customer, order, subject, description, status open|in_review|resolved|rejected, response, resolvedBy)

## Models owned by others (reference with ref only, never redefine)
User, Branch, Employee (Member 1), MenuItem, Order (Member 3).
server/models/User.js is a TEMPORARY stub until Member 1 delivers the real one.
middleware/auth.js (protect, authorize) is a TEMPORARY stub; keep the same export names.

## Conventions
- API response format: { success: boolean, data, message }
- Controllers use async/await with try/catch and next(err); central error handler in server.js
- Routes in routes/*.js, mounted in server.js as /api/<resource>
- Define static routes like /me BEFORE /:id routes
- Protect routes with protect, then authorize(...roles)
- Secrets only in server/.env (MONGO_URI, JWT_SECRET, PORT=5000). Never commit .env. Keep .env.example updated
- Frontend calls the API only through client/src/api/axios.js
- Keep code simple, readable, beginner-friendly, with short comments

